# TEMPLATE for caddy/tokens.caddy.
#
# The real file (caddy/tokens.caddy) is NOT versioned: it contains each person's
# tokens and cookies. scripts/token.sh generates it:
#
#     ./scripts/token.sh add <name> [expiry]
#
# This matcher is the valid state with ZERO credentials: nobody gets in. It lets
# a new clone bring the stack up before granting access:
#
#     cp caddy/tokens.caddy.example caddy/tokens.caddy
#
# (If you start docker without the file existing, Docker creates a DIRECTORY in
# its place and the mount breaks. That is why this cp is worth it.)

@gate expression `false`
@canje expression `false`
